        rdfs:comment                   "PRIESTS'S HOOD\nCHINESE or CENTRAL ASIAN; 18th-19th century.\nEmbroidered in silk and gilt thread on satin: lined with Chinese silk. []"@en , "Hood, embroidered silk, China, 1750-1899"@en , "This is a windproof hat meant to be worn for protection against cold weather. Although it has imperial symbols as decoration (e.g. a dragon and stylised waves), it may not have been worn by an important member of the royal family."@en , "Yellow hat, embroidered with an dragon over a simple waves and mountain (<i>haishui jiangya</i>) motif. Lined with red silk."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/b58b49f7-1125-3d04-b7d3-751598f3af14> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "PRIESTS'S HOOD\nCHINESE or CENTRAL ASIAN; 18th-19th century.\nEmbroidered in silk and gilt thread on satin: lined with Chinese silk. []"@en , "Hood, embroidered silk, China, 1750-1899"@en , "This is a windproof hat meant to be worn for protection against cold weather. Although it has imperial symbols as decoration (e.g. a dragon and stylised waves), it may not have been worn by an important member of the royal family."@en , "Yellow hat, embroidered with an dragon over a simple waves and mountain (<i>haishui jiangya</i>) motif. Lined with red silk."@en ;
